body:
Running the MRP I get undefined behaviour. Which makes total sense, taking a closer look at your function, you can see clearly that you have created a situation where the function may not return anything at all:

```
if ( eye_dir.y < 0.0 && camera_position.y > plane_position.y )
if ( tiling || max(abs(tuv.x),abs(tuv.y)) < 0.5 )
return texture(plane_texture, tuv+vec2(0.5));
```

The only return statement is at the end of the function, but it is behind to `if` statements, if either of those `if` statements fail, then the function won't have anything to return, so it will return uninitialized memory. This is _undefined behaviour_ which means that the GPU driver gets to decide what happens. We have no control over its behaviour. My guess is that on your device the driver decides to always return ` texture(plane_texture, tuv+vec2(0.5))` and basically ignore your if statements, other devices try to respect the if statements and return uninitialized memory while other devices fail to compile altogether and give a black screen as a result.
